        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Nehemiah 12:20",
        "book": "Nehemiah",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Of Hilkiah, Hashabiah; of Jedaiah, Nethaneel.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Nehemiah 12:21",
        "book": "Nehemiah",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "The Levites in the days of Eliashib, Joiada, and Johanan, and Jaddua, were recorded chief of the fathers: also the priests, to the reign of Darius the Persian.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 74
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Nehemiah 12:22",
        "book": "Nehemiah",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "The sons of Levi, the chief of the fathers, were written in the book of the chronicles, even until the days of Johanan the son of Eliashib.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Nehemiah 12:23",
        "book": "Nehemiah",
        "chapter": 12,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And the chief of the Levites: Hashabiah, Sherebiah, and Jeshua the son of Kadmiel, with their brethren over against them, to praise and to give thanks, according to the commandment of David the man of God, ward over against ward.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 144,
            "end": 150,
            "text": "D&C 59:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 135
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "D&C 59:21.",
            "prettyString": "D&C 59:21",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "doctrineandcovenants",
                "chapters": [
                  {
